WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.766
- Pik? Pika?
- Hm? I wonder what that noise was.

2
00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:11.066
Huh? What noise?

3
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.533
I didn’t hear anything.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:16.966
- Hm.
- Na, Na!

5
00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.900
Maybe you imagined it.

6
00:00:18.966 --> 00:00:21.966
No. I definitely heard something.

7
00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.900
Hm...

8
00:00:25.966 --> 00:00:27.466
-Huh?

9
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:31.466
- Was that...?
- Both of your tummies are rumbling!

10
00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.033
Huh?

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.433
Wait a minute. I hear something now.

12
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.933
Huh?

13
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.599
Whoa!

14
00:00:52.066 --> 00:00:55.199
- That was close.
- What is that guy’s problem?

15
00:00:55.266 --> 00:00:58.466
Out of the way!

16
00:00:58.533 --> 00:00:59.766
Whoa!

17
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:02.400
If Officer Jenny’s after that guy...

18
00:01:02.466 --> 00:01:05.833
Then that crazy driver could possibly be a wanted criminal!

19
00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.033
There could be trouble!

20
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.933
- Let’s go and check it out!
- Pikachu!

21
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.700
♪ I want to be the very best ♪

22
00:01:12.766 --> 00:01:16.500
♪ Like no one ever was ♪

23
00:01:16.566 --> 00:01:19.233
♪ To catch them is my real test ♪

24
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.233
♪ To train them is my cause ♪

25
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.300
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all It's you and me ♪

26
00:01:25.366 --> 00:01:28.500
♪ Pokémon! I know it's my destiny ♪

27
00:01:28.566 --> 00:01:31.933
♪ Pokémon! Yeah, you're my best friend ♪

28
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.366
♪ In a world we must defend ♪

29
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:36.866
♪ Pokémon! Got to catch them all ♪

30
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.933
♪ Got to catch them all! Pokémon! ♪

31
00:01:49.466 --> 00:01:52.166
As our heroes continue their journey to Cyllage City

32
00:01:52.233 --> 00:01:54.000
and Ash’s next Kalos Gym battle,

33
00:01:54.066 --> 00:01:58.133
they’ve witnessed a police chase and now rush to assist Officer Jenny!

34
00:01:58.199 --> 00:02:01.033
-Hey! Stop the car!

35
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.500
Like I’m going to listen to what you say! Give me a break, Jenny!

36
00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:07.033
Come back here!

37
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.566
- Diggersby, use Mud Shot!
- Diggersby!

38
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:13.233
Diggersby!

39
00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:20.766
-See you later!

40
00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:24.933
Diggersby!

41
00:02:27.366 --> 00:02:32.433
My valuable merchandise! It fell off! It can’t be! No!

42
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.100
Come back here!

43
00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.066
Oh! Oh! I can’t go on!

44
00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:41.799
- Clemont! Get a grip!
- Na! Na!

45
00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:45.233
- Are you all right?
- Uh, Clemont, how are you doing?

46
00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:48.733
Huh? Something’s crawling out of there.

47
00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.799
- Scatter?
- Never seen that before.

48
00:02:54.866 --> 00:02:57.566
Scatterbug. the Scatterdust Pokémon.

49
00:02:57.633 --> 00:03:01.166
When attacked by another Pokémon, Scatterbug scatters the black powder

50
00:03:01.233 --> 00:03:04.366
that covers its body and regulates its body temperature.

51
00:03:04.433 --> 00:03:05.666
Scatterbug!

52
00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:08.266
It looks like it’s trying to scare us off.

53
00:03:08.333 --> 00:03:12.000
You don’t have to worry about us hurting you, Scatterbug. We’re your friends!

54
00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:14.233
- Pikachu!
- Scatter!

55
00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:17.966
- Oh! Scatterbug!
- Scatterbug looks kind of weak.

56
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.166
We’d better hurry and take it to a Pokémon Center!

57
00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:24.466
I’ll look it up. It’s over this way! Come on!

58
00:03:24.533 --> 00:03:26.833
- Okay, let’s go!
- Pika, Pika!

59
00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:34.766
Huh? Huh?

60
00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:39.633
- Nurse Joy, please help Scatterbug!
- Sure!

61
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:43.533
- Take care of it, Wigglytuff!
- Wigglytuff!

62
00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.633
- Now, don’t worry about a thing.
- Thanks a lot!

63
00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.633
It looks like your Scatterbug doesn’t come from around this area.

64
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.133
Huh? Wait, you can tell just by looking?

65
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.899
Yes! Take a look up at the screen.

66
00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:57.633
Huh?

67
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.366
- Wow, Vivillon!
- But they all look different.

68
00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:04.700
Vivillon have many different patterns, depending on where they come from

69
00:04:04.766 --> 00:04:07.299
and there are many more patterns than that!

70
00:04:07.366 --> 00:04:08.566
Awesome!

71
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:12.100
In a similar way, Scatterbug have slight differences, too.

72
00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:13.200
- Wow!
- Pika!

73
00:04:13.266 --> 00:04:16.766
I’d be very interested to know where you found that Scatterbug.

74
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:19.700
- Well... Whoa!
- I've got you!

75
00:04:19.766 --> 00:04:22.733
Now, don’t make a move, or you’ll be in a whole lot more trouble

76
00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.966
than you’re already in!

77
00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.633
Move? You’ve already got me tied up!

78
00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.599
Believe me, I know who you are! If you have the stolen Scatterbug,

79
00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:34.300
then you must work with Dolan, the Pokémon smuggler!

80
00:04:34.366 --> 00:04:36.366
- Pokémon smuggler?!
- No way!

81
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:40.533
We were chasing after you because we wanted to help you, Officer Jenny!

82
00:04:40.599 --> 00:04:44.833
On the way, we found a big cage and Scatterbug was coming out of it!

83
00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.533
Then that means...

84
00:04:46.599 --> 00:04:49.966
Somehow, the Pokémon smuggler must have dropped the cage.

85
00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:53.333
- That’s what I think.
- Oh, I’m so sorry!

86
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.400
I’m always jumping to conclusions and then I mess things up.

87
00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.933
- Manectric!
- Don’t worry. It’s okay!

88
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.466
- Huh?

89
00:05:03.533 --> 00:05:06.500
- Scatterbug’s fine now!
- Bug Scat!

90
00:05:06.566 --> 00:05:09.599
- Scatterbug!
- You’re okay!

91
00:05:10.966 --> 00:05:13.366
All that stuff you were talking about earlier,

92
00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:16.133
I never heard of a Pokémon smuggler before!

93
00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:20.599
Pokémon smugglers are bad people who steal and then sell Pokémon online

94
00:05:20.666 --> 00:05:23.366
to unscrupulous Pokémon collectors the world over.

95
00:05:23.433 --> 00:05:26.466
- First they steal Pokémon?
- Then they sell them online?

96
00:05:26.533 --> 00:05:31.233
Right. Dolan’s a Pokémon smuggler. He specializes in Vivillon,

97
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:35.233
so he grabs every Scatterbug and Spewpa he can get his thieving hands on.

98
00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.900
So, he must be keeping lots of them at his hideout!

99
00:05:37.966 --> 00:05:41.400
All those poor, helpless Scatterbug and Spewpa...

100
00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:44.599
Yes, I’m sure he’s got countless Pokémon.

101
00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:47.900
And once they evolve into Vivillon, he sells them at a premium.

102
00:05:47.966 --> 00:05:49.900
There’s no excuse for that!

103
00:05:49.966 --> 00:05:52.233
- What an awful guy!
- Pikachu!

104
00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.300
- The worst!
- He stinks!

105
00:05:54.366 --> 00:05:56.833
- Disgusting!
- Hm! Huh?

106
00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.033
Scatterbug is getting restless.

107
00:05:59.099 --> 00:06:00.900
Scatter, Scatter, Scatter!

108
00:06:00.966 --> 00:06:03.433
- Sca...
- Huh?

109
00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.333
Look!

110
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.733
Spewpa!

111
00:06:08.766 --> 00:06:12.766
I’ve never seen a Pokémon evolve right in front of my eyes!

112
00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:16.733
Spewpa, the Scatterdust Pokémon. When Spewpa is attacked, it scares

113
00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.466
its enemies away by stiffening and spreading its fur, like wings.

114
00:06:20.533 --> 00:06:22.400
Spwep!

115
00:06:22.466 --> 00:06:24.633
Hey, since we just saw Scatterbug evolve,

116
00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.400
could you teach me about Evolution, please?

117
00:06:27.466 --> 00:06:30.166
- I can do that! No prob!
- Pika, Pika!

118
00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:35.033
Evolution is when a Pokémon starts to glow super bright and transform like bam!

119
00:06:35.099 --> 00:06:37.833
And that’s when everyone goes, "Wow, that’s awesome!"

120
00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.766
- That’s about all there is to it.
- Pika Pikachu!

121
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:45.266
- Okay, I don’t get it at all.
- I guess that’s my cue to take over!

122
00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:47.500
There are some kinds of Pokémon

123
00:06:47.566 --> 00:06:50.833
who change their shapes after certain criteria are met

124
00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.900
and this is called Evolution.

125
00:06:52.966 --> 00:06:58.033
For example, Scatterbug evolves into Spewpa and Spewpa evolves into Vivillon.

126
00:06:58.099 --> 00:07:02.666
There are several ways to make Pokémon evolve, but the most common way is,

127
00:07:02.733 --> 00:07:06.833
like with Vivillon, when they reach a certain level and then evolve.

128
00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.333
An alternative method is by using an Evolution Stone.

129
00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.900
For example, for Pikachu to evolve into Raichu,

130
00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.333
- it needs a Thunder Stone.
- Rain!

131
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.833
Ah! It’s so amazing how they evolve.

132
00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.566
Mm-hm! Pokémon sure are amazing! I guess I’ve still got a lot to learn!

133
00:07:24.633 --> 00:07:28.433
Clemont was saying what I was saying in a different way.

134
00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.566
Pikachu!

135
00:07:29.633 --> 00:07:33.299
- You think?
- That was great. Thank you very much!

136
00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:37.000
Think nothing of it. Impressive, eh? Hm?

137
00:07:37.066 --> 00:07:40.000
There seems to be something in Spewpa’s fur.

138
00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:43.900
- Yeah, I wonder what it could be?
- Let’s take a closer look!

139
00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:49.000
It looks like some sort of chip that’s used for transmitting signals!

140
00:07:49.066 --> 00:07:51.799
A signal? But for what?

141
00:07:51.866 --> 00:07:55.566
I know! Dolan must have implanted that chip as a tracking device,

142
00:07:55.633 --> 00:07:59.366
so he could hunt down any Pokémon that might get away from him!

143
00:07:59.433 --> 00:08:01.700
Then he might be close by!

144
00:08:01.766 --> 00:08:04.066
Well, if he is, I’ll get him!

145
00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:07.266
- Pikachu!
- Spew, Spew, Spewpa!

146
00:08:07.333 --> 00:08:10.700
- Huh? What’s wrong?
- Spewpa’s probably worried.

147
00:08:10.766 --> 00:08:14.866
After all, Dolan is still holding its friends captive.

148
00:08:14.933 --> 00:08:18.066
You want to get your friends out of there, right?

149
00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:20.166
- I’ve got a great idea!
- Huh?

150
00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.466
First, we’ll let Dolan take Spewpa back

151
00:08:22.533 --> 00:08:24.666
and then we’ll follow, using the transmitter’s signal.

152
00:08:24.733 --> 00:08:28.299
That way, he’ll lead us to the hideout and all the Pokémon, too!

153
00:08:28.366 --> 00:08:31.166
And that’ll make it easy to rescue all of Spewpa’s stolen friends!

154
00:08:31.233 --> 00:08:34.600
That’s a great plan! Do you think we can really pull it off?

155
00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:36.666
We happen to have an inventor in the house!

156
00:08:36.733 --> 00:08:39.566
- Sounds like my cue to get busy!
- Huh?

157
00:08:39.633 --> 00:08:43.566
The future is now, thanks to science!

158
00:08:43.633 --> 00:08:45.566
Clemontic Gear, On!

159
00:08:45.633 --> 00:08:50.600
I happen to have the perfect invention for just a situation like this and here it is!

160
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:54.066
I like to call it the Omni-Directional Super-Sensitive Tracking Dish!

161
00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.600
Huh?

162
00:08:56.666 --> 00:08:59.066
- The name’s better this time.
- Na, Na!

163
00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:01.733
The first thing we need to do is detect

164
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.300
and memorize the frequency of the transmitter chip.

165
00:09:05.366 --> 00:09:11.100
We can then pinpoint Spewpa’s location, no matter where it goes! Power on!

166
00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:13.033
See! We’re up and running!

167
00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.333
- Awesome! Science is so amazing!
- Pika, Pika!

168
00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:18.833
But Dolan dropped Scatterbug, right?

169
00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:22.066
Remember, Scatterbug evolved into Spewpa since then.

170
00:09:22.133 --> 00:09:23.633
Spewpa!

171
00:09:23.699 --> 00:09:28.033
Don’t worry! No problem! Once he sees Scatterbug’s chip on Spewpa,

172
00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.566
it won’t take him long to figure everything out.

173
00:09:30.633 --> 00:09:35.500
I feel uncomfortable about all this. Maybe we shouldn’t be using Spewpa as bait.

174
00:09:35.566 --> 00:09:38.500
- It’s dangerous!
- I’ll just act as a decoy!

175
00:09:38.566 --> 00:09:41.133
Well, if anybody can pull it off, it’s you!

176
00:09:41.199 --> 00:09:43.300
- Thanks!
- Just a minute!

177
00:09:43.366 --> 00:09:45.900
I thought of this, so I want to help!

178
00:09:45.966 --> 00:09:51.100
- Costume designing is what I do!
- The master of makeup!

179
00:09:53.699 --> 00:09:57.166
Spew, Spew, Spewpa!

180
00:09:57.233 --> 00:10:01.333
You definitely look like Spewpa, but you’re a bit too big!

181
00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:02.766
Spew!

182
00:10:02.833 --> 00:10:06.666
Plus, you won’t be able to fit inside the cage we found Scatterbug in.

183
00:10:06.733 --> 00:10:08.000
Na, Na!

184
00:10:08.066 --> 00:10:11.900
- Let’s have Dedenne do it!
- Huh? Yay! Dedenne!

185
00:10:11.966 --> 00:10:14.266
Spewpa!

186
00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:17.066
You might just be the tiniest bit too teeny.

187
00:10:17.133 --> 00:10:19.300
Then how about using my Chespin?!

188
00:10:20.366 --> 00:10:24.566
- It’s just the right size!
- Ches, Chespin! Chespin!

189
00:10:24.633 --> 00:10:27.766
-Looks just like Spewpa!

190
00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:36.166
All we do now is wait for Dolan to show up.

191
00:10:36.233 --> 00:10:39.966
Unless he makes an appearance, the whole plan will be rendered useless.

192
00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:41.666
Dolan’s a very greedy man.

193
00:10:41.733 --> 00:10:44.833
He’ll definitely come back, or he won’t make all that money.

194
00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.699
Once he makes his pickup, we’ll follow.

195
00:10:47.766 --> 00:10:50.466
Then we can track him down to his hideout!

196
00:10:50.533 --> 00:10:52.199
Look! It’s him!

197
00:10:59.933 --> 00:11:02.300
Who’s that Pokémon?

198
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.666
It’s Scatterbug!

199
00:11:19.266 --> 00:11:23.233
The signal from the chip’s coming from here, somewhere.

200
00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:28.166
There you are! Is my precious merchandise safe and sound?

201
00:11:28.233 --> 00:11:29.733
Ches... Pin...

202
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.633
So you evolved into a Spewpa, eh?

203
00:11:32.699 --> 00:11:35.900
Though you do look and sound a bit strange.

204
00:11:35.966 --> 00:11:40.833
Maybe now you’ll evolve into a hugely profitable Vivillon!

205
00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.733
It looks like Dolan bought the disguise.

206
00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.933
- I know what I’m doing.
- Hm!

207
00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.233
Off we go!

208
00:11:50.466 --> 00:11:53.600
- Well, Clemont?
- My invention’s working great!

209
00:11:53.666 --> 00:11:56.266
- Ready to go?
- Yeah! Let’s move it!

210
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.000
- Dolan just drove into the forest!
- We can’t lose him!

211
00:12:07.066 --> 00:12:10.866
Don’t worry. As long as the chip is sending a signal... Whoa!

212
00:12:10.933 --> 00:12:14.966
- What’s wrong?
- I don’t know! What happened?!

213
00:12:21.666 --> 00:12:26.366
All right, then. I’ll just have to follow him. Thanks for your help!

214
00:12:26.433 --> 00:12:29.266
Huh? Good luck!

215
00:12:29.333 --> 00:12:31.800
Spew! Hey. We’ll save all your buddies.

216
00:12:31.866 --> 00:12:33.933
- I promise!
- Pika!

217
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.800
- Maybe your Fletchling can search for him!
- Yeah! Fletchling, I choose you!

218
00:12:40.233 --> 00:12:43.699
- Fletch! Fletchling!
- I need you to look for a vehicle!

219
00:12:43.766 --> 00:12:45.033
Fletching!

220
00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:51.800
Fletch! Fletchling!

221
00:12:54.133 --> 00:12:56.300
- Fletch!
- Find it?

222
00:12:56.366 --> 00:12:59.166
- Fletchling!
- Show us where it is!

223
00:12:59.233 --> 00:13:00.833
Fletch!

224
00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:12.166
What’s wrong? Maybe Dolan’s hideout is nearby.

225
00:13:12.233 --> 00:13:14.233
- Fletchling!
- Fletchling, did you find it?

226
00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.766
- Fletch, Fletch!
- Great! Return!

227
00:13:21.099 --> 00:13:25.199
- That’s definitely it! Dolan’s truck!
- And no one’s guarding the hideout.

228
00:13:25.266 --> 00:13:27.333
Wonder where Officer Jenny is.

229
00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.699
Hm. Let’s sit tight for now.

230
00:13:29.766 --> 00:13:33.500
But what if he escapes while we’re waiting for her? Let’s go!

231
00:13:33.566 --> 00:13:38.266
Wait! If Dolan sees us coming, who knows what he’ll do to the Pokémon?

232
00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:41.133
Serena’s right. We need to make safely rescuing

233
00:13:41.199 --> 00:13:43.533
the captive Pokémon our first priority!

234
00:13:43.599 --> 00:13:45.066
Then what are we supposed to do?

235
00:13:45.133 --> 00:13:47.366
We should find out if anyone’s inside.

236
00:13:47.433 --> 00:13:50.066
Got it! Now, Froakie, I choose you!

237
00:13:51.599 --> 00:13:53.066
Froakie!

238
00:13:53.133 --> 00:13:57.166
I need you to find out if there’s anyone inside that building.

239
00:13:57.233 --> 00:14:01.599
- If no one’s in there, use this sign!
- Kie! Fro!

240
00:14:01.666 --> 00:14:03.966
Froakie!

241
00:14:04.033 --> 00:14:07.866
Fro! Fro! Fro! Kie!

242
00:14:07.933 --> 00:14:10.466
Fro! Fro! Fro!

243
00:14:10.533 --> 00:14:13.533
Fro? Fro! Kie?

244
00:14:13.599 --> 00:14:15.099
Fro!

245
00:14:20.366 --> 00:14:22.033
Kie!

246
00:14:23.033 --> 00:14:24.133
Fro!

247
00:14:24.199 --> 00:14:26.633
Froakie’s saying the coast is all clear!

248
00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:28.133
That means now’s our chance!

249
00:14:28.199 --> 00:14:31.300
Okay! Let’s get in there and rescue the Pokémon!

250
00:14:31.366 --> 00:14:33.300
- Yay!
- Na, Na, Na!

251
00:14:33.366 --> 00:14:35.166
Pikachu!

252
00:14:38.699 --> 00:14:40.633
- Spew!
- Mm? Something wrong?

253
00:14:43.433 --> 00:14:45.433
- Pikachu!
- Pikachu! Everybody!

254
00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.233
Well, well, well. Guess I missed a Pokémon and some kid.

255
00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.433
- Dolan!
- How about that? Heard of me, huh?

256
00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.966
- Let all my friends go!
- Give me a break!

257
00:14:55.033 --> 00:14:57.433
Nobody tricks me and gets away with it!

258
00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.599
You punks are responsible for this, aren’t you?

259
00:14:59.666 --> 00:15:01.366
Ah! It's Chespin!

260
00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:04.199
It was a rough ride, so the disguise fell off,

261
00:15:04.266 --> 00:15:07.633
but I’ll get even with you by selling this little one, too!

262
00:15:07.699 --> 00:15:10.000
-You’re not doing that!

263
00:15:10.066 --> 00:15:15.066
You’ve got some mouth on you! Now, hand over that Spewpa!

264
00:15:15.133 --> 00:15:17.966
- Diggersby!
- Who’s that Pokémon?!

265
00:15:18.033 --> 00:15:22.533
Diggersby, the Digging Pokémon and the evolved form of Bunnelby.

266
00:15:22.599 --> 00:15:24.333
Diggersby can easily lift a boulder

267
00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.733
weighing over a ton with its powerful ears.

268
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.833
-Froakie.

269
00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.233
- Want to battle?
- Fro!

270
00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:32.166
Diggersby’s a Ground type!

271
00:15:32.233 --> 00:15:35.366
So Froakie’s Water-type moves are super effective against it!

272
00:15:35.433 --> 00:15:37.699
- I know you can do it, Ash!
- Na! Na!

273
00:15:37.766 --> 00:15:40.566
- Don’t lose to a crook like him!
- Pikapi!

274
00:15:40.633 --> 00:15:42.533
Right! He's going down!

275
00:15:42.599 --> 00:15:44.400
We’ll just see about that!

276
00:15:44.466 --> 00:15:46.866
Diggersby, Mud Shot!

277
00:15:46.933 --> 00:15:48.933
Diggersby!

278
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.366
- Dodge, Froakie!
- Fro! Froakie!

279
00:15:52.433 --> 00:15:54.233
Great! Use Bubble!

280
00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.466
Kie! Fro!

281
00:15:58.566 --> 00:16:00.166
What?! Use Dig!

282
00:16:02.466 --> 00:16:06.666
Ah! It can come out from anywhere! Be careful and stay focused!

283
00:16:06.733 --> 00:16:08.500
Fro?

284
00:16:08.566 --> 00:16:10.866
- Froakie!
- Double Slap, let’s go!

285
00:16:10.933 --> 00:16:13.566
Froakie won’t be able to dodge if it’s in the air!

286
00:16:13.633 --> 00:16:15.433
Diggersby!

287
00:16:17.233 --> 00:16:18.866
You’re doing great!

288
00:16:18.933 --> 00:16:21.800
- Great! Prove them wrong with Hammer Arm!
- Digger!

289
00:16:21.866 --> 00:16:26.666
- Use Water Pulse and counter that!
- Froakie!

290
00:16:26.733 --> 00:16:30.266
Dig! Dig! Dig!

291
00:16:30.333 --> 00:16:33.666
Fro! Fro!

292
00:16:33.733 --> 00:16:35.766
Froakie! Be strong!

293
00:16:35.833 --> 00:16:39.333
Ha-ha! Isn’t that sweet? Enough of this!

294
00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:42.766
Use Hammer Arm and attack as hard as you can!

295
00:16:42.833 --> 00:16:45.666
- Froakie! Are you okay?
- Froak!

296
00:16:45.733 --> 00:16:50.133
Hey, Spewpa! Don’t worry! I’m going to keep you safe, no matter what!

297
00:16:50.199 --> 00:16:53.900
Spewpa!

298
00:16:53.966 --> 00:16:57.099
Oh! Spewpa! You’re protecting both of us!

299
00:16:57.166 --> 00:17:00.566
- Spew!
- Don’t forget, that’s my merchandise!

300
00:17:00.633 --> 00:17:02.066
Enough! Forget it!

301
00:17:02.133 --> 00:17:06.433
Use Hammer Arm and show that Spewpa who it’s messing with!

302
00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.166
Spewpa!

303
00:17:08.233 --> 00:17:13.066
It’s Spewpa’s Protect! Nice job, Spewpa!

304
00:17:13.133 --> 00:17:15.733
That’s String Shot!

305
00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.933
- Wow, Spewpa! you’re awesome!
- A Diggersby mummy!

306
00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.300
- Pika!
- Na, Na!

307
00:17:20.366 --> 00:17:22.899
What do you think you’re doing? Get out of that!

308
00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:28.233
- Oh!
- Now, I think it’s time we finish this up!

309
00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:32.233
- Hey, Spewpa, what’s the matter?
- Spew, Spew, Spew! Ah!

310
00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.966
Of course! When Spewpa starts getting restless, that means...

311
00:17:36.033 --> 00:17:38.000
Spew, Spew, Spew, Spew!

312
00:17:38.066 --> 00:17:39.733
It’s evolving!

313
00:17:43.633 --> 00:17:47.100
On! Vivillon!

314
00:17:47.166 --> 00:17:49.866
- Wow! So cool!
- Vi!

315
00:17:49.933 --> 00:17:53.600
It has a different pattern than the Vivillon Viola had!

316
00:17:53.666 --> 00:17:55.466
Vi, Vi, Vi!

317
00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:57.399
- Pretty!
- Pika!

318
00:17:57.466 --> 00:18:01.966
Gorgeous! Vivillon’s beauty is what makes them fetch such a high price!

319
00:18:02.033 --> 00:18:04.033
Scatterbug and Spewpa!

320
00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:08.200
They’re all fantastic moneymakers!

321
00:18:08.266 --> 00:18:12.966
Oh, man. That guy! You only think of Pokémon as a way to make money!

322
00:18:13.033 --> 00:18:15.200
Hurry up and get rid of that annoying kid

323
00:18:15.266 --> 00:18:18.200
with the big mouth or I’ll go nuts! Mud Shot go!

324
00:18:18.266 --> 00:18:20.866
-Oh! Come on!

325
00:18:20.933 --> 00:18:25.933
- It’s Vivillon’s Safeguard!
- That's great, Vivillon! Go!

326
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.666
Vi! Vi, Vi, Vi, Vi, Vi, Vi, Vi !

327
00:18:28.733 --> 00:18:31.433
Ah! It’s Stun Spore!

328
00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.700
Diggersby!

329
00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:44.200
Huh? Diggersby! All right, I’ll just catch you myself!

330
00:18:44.266 --> 00:18:46.633
What’s that?

331
00:18:47.633 --> 00:18:51.233
- Officer Jenny!
- Sorry to keep you waiting!

332
00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:53.833
No, you don’t!

333
00:18:53.899 --> 00:18:58.333
Stop! Or prepare for an Electro Ball! See?

334
00:18:58.399 --> 00:19:02.766
If you still think I’m going to listen to anything you say, give me a break!

335
00:19:02.833 --> 00:19:03.966
Huh?

336
00:19:04.033 --> 00:19:05.399
- Vi, Vi, Vi!
- Huh?

337
00:19:05.466 --> 00:19:08.899
Uh! I’m starting to feel like I should give up.

338
00:19:08.966 --> 00:19:11.333
Vivillon’s scales have a soothing effect

339
00:19:11.399 --> 00:19:13.399
that calms an opponent’s fighting spirit!

340
00:19:13.466 --> 00:19:15.933
Now you’re under arrest!

341
00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.399
Okay, I give up.

342
00:19:18.466 --> 00:19:22.133
- Chespin, you were great!
- Chespin!

343
00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.399
Vivillon!

344
00:19:23.466 --> 00:19:26.833
Yeah. Let’s get the others out of there!

345
00:19:32.666 --> 00:19:34.700
Okay, everyone! You’re free now!

346
00:19:37.766 --> 00:19:40.899
Vivillon looks really happy to see its friends again.

347
00:19:40.966 --> 00:19:43.333
It’s great to see all of you together!

348
00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:44.500
Vivillon!

349
00:19:44.566 --> 00:19:46.933
Spewpa!

350
00:19:55.766 --> 00:20:02.700
Vi, Vi, Vi, Vivillon!

351
00:20:02.766 --> 00:20:06.166
Hey, everyone! Don’t get caught again!

352
00:20:06.233 --> 00:20:08.100
Pika, Pika!

353
00:20:08.166 --> 00:20:12.000
Vi, Vi, Vi, Vivillon!

354
00:20:12.066 --> 00:20:13.866
Vivillon!

355
00:20:13.933 --> 00:20:15.899
Bye! See you again!

356
00:20:15.966 --> 00:20:18.500
Vi, Vi, Vivillon!

357
00:20:18.566 --> 00:20:21.500
Vivillon!

358
00:20:21.566 --> 00:20:25.000
Vivillon are so beautiful!

359
00:20:25.066 --> 00:20:30.866
Vi, Vi, Vi, Vivillon!

360
00:20:33.966 --> 00:20:35.866
With the help of Officer Jenny,

361
00:20:35.933 --> 00:20:40.200
our heroes have stopped the horrendous deeds of Pokémon smuggler Dolan

362
00:20:40.266 --> 00:20:42.200
and freed the stolen Vivillon.

363
00:20:42.266 --> 00:20:45.933
Now, the journey to Cyllage City continues!
